      "edition": "Thursday 29 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Welsh rugby shake-up",
          "heading": "WRU in talks with Premiership and RFU over two Welsh clubs joining",
          "body": "Welsh rugby's structure may be about to change again: WalesOnline understands the WRU is in negotiations with Premiership Rugby and the RFU over two Welsh clubs joining the Gallagher Prem. The move could come as early as next season, though the following campaign is considered more realistic. For the Ospreys and Scarlets, already fighting to survive a proposed cut from four regions to three, it could change everything. The WRU's statement still commits to four URC teams until the end of 2027/28."
        },
        {
