      "edition": "Thursday 29 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad recall",
          "heading": "Les Kiss recalls Kurtley Beale, 37, five years after last Test",
          "body": "Les Kiss has reached for a 95-Test veteran, calling Kurtley Beale into the squad to replace Hunter Paisami, who is unavailable for personal reasons. It is Beale’s first Wallabies squad since 2024, when an Achilles injury ended his season, and his last Test came against Wales in Cardiff in 2021. “With Hunter’s unavailability we’re excited by what Kurtley can bring to the group,” Kiss said. Beale will primarily cover inside centre, and Kiss has also pointed to his form for the Western Force."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa without Kolbe and Etzebeth through injury for Nations Championship",
